-- title:
--   Faithful flatness of O^{nr} over a discrete valuation ring
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal{O}$ be a commutative ring which is an integral domain, assumed to be a discrete valuation ring (the hypothesis `hdvr` being the relevant `IsDiscreteValuationRing` statement), let $\pi \in \mathcal{O}$ be an irreducible element, and let $O^{nr}$ be a commutative ring which is an integral domain and an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra. Assume that the structure map $\mathcal{O} \to O^{nr}$ is injective, and that the ideal of $O^{nr}$ generated by the image of $\pi$ is proper, i.e. not the whole of $O^{nr}$. Then $O^{nr}$ is a faithfully flat $\mathcal{O}$-module, in the sense of Mathlib's `Module.FaithfullyFlat`: it is flat over $\mathcal{O}$ and, in addition, satisfies the non-degeneracy condition recorded by that class (equivalently, flat together with $I \cdot O^{nr} \ne O^{nr}$ for every proper ideal $I$ of $\mathcal{O}$). Note that only irreducibility of $\pi$, injectivity of the structure map and properness of $\pi O^{nr}$ are assumed; no unramifiedness, completeness or finiteness hypothesis on $O^{nr}$ enters.
--
--   This is the standard criterion that a torsion-free algebra over a discrete valuation ring in which the uniformiser stays a non-unit is faithfully flat; it is applied with $O^{nr}$ the maximal unramified (or completed unramified) extension of the base ring. It is one of the generic inputs to the flat-descent lifting steps for the Čerednik–Drinfeld uniformisation, being cited by [`CerednikDrinfeld.QM.IsFineModuli.exists_flat_family_lift_of_cerednikDrinfeld_uniformization_fine`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.QM.IsFineModuli.exists_flat_family_lift_of_cerednikDrinfeld_uniformization_fine), [`CerednikDrinfeld.QM.exists_flat_family_lift_of_formallyEtale_of_locallyOfFiniteType`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.QM.exists_flat_family_lift_of_formallyEtale_of_locallyOfFiniteType) and [`CerednikDrinfeld.FormalOmega.eq_of_natural_of_forall_eq_of_comp_mk_eq_comp_val`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.FormalOmega.eq_of_natural_of_forall_eq_of_comp_mk_eq_comp_val).
